PEP 440 strips leading zeroes from numeric local version segments, so a short
SHA such as 07243313 is rendered as 7243313.  The fixed-length regexp in this
test therefore fails whenever the generated commit hash starts with zero.

Compare against the normalized short SHA instead, which keeps the assertion
deterministic while still checking that the dev template is used.

--- a/tests/test_integration/test_scikit_build_metadata.py
+++ b/tests/test_integration/test_scikit_build_metadata.py
@@ -1,15 +1,15 @@
